> <volume>51</volume>:<fpage>71</fpage>&#x02013;84.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16815333</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Walther, K., M.K. Diril, N. Jung, and V. Haucke. <year>2004</year>. Functional dissection of the interactions of stonin 2 with the adaptor complex AP-2 and synaptotagmin. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>101</volume>:<fpage>964</fpage>&#x02013;969.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14726597</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib39"><citation citation-type="journal">Wienisch, M., and J. Klingauf. <year>2006</year>. Vesicular proteins exocytosed and subsequently retrieved by compensatory endocytosis are nonidentical. <source>Nat. Neurosci.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>1019</fpage>&#x02013;1027.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16845386</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib40"><citation citation-type="journal">Willig, K.I., S.O. Rizzoli, V. Westphal, R. Jahn, and S.W. Hell. <year>2006</year>. STED microscopy reveals that synaptotagmin remains clustered after synaptic vesicle exocytosis. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>440</volume>:<fpage>935</fpage>&#x02013;939.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16612384</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, A., J.F. Rual, K. Tamai, Y. Harada, M. Vidal, X. He, and T. Kirchhausen. <year>2007</year>. Association of dishevelled with the clathrin ap-2 adaptor is required for frizzled endocytosis and planar cell polarity signaling. <source>Dev. Cell.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>129</fpage>&#x02013;141.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17199046</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Zhang, J.Z., B.A. Davletov, T.C. Sudhof, and R.G. Anderson. <year>1994</year>. Synaptotagmin I is a high affinity receptor for clathrin AP-2: implications for membrane recycling. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>78</volume>:<fpage>751</fpage>&#x02013;760.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8087843</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></